WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.980
A lighthouse beam holds
steady over a stormy sea.

2
00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:06.090
Waves smash against it.

3
00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.260
The light never moves.

4
00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:12.740
High above, one bright star
hangs over a small sailing ship,

5
00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:14.420
lost in the dark.

6
00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.290
An hourglass runs.

7
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:19.510
A sickle sweeps across a field of flowers.

8
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.630
And yet, "Love’s not Time’s fool".

9
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:26.620
Twelve lines insist that
true love never changes.

10
00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:30.850
Then the last two begin
with one small word: If.

11
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.260
So why end on If?

12
00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:36.340
In this mission, you'll test
the sonnet's sea images,

13
00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.610
the fixed mark and the star.

14
00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:41.960
You'll meet Time, a reaper
with a "bending sickle".

15
00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:45.070
And you'll see how fourteen
lines build an argument,

16
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.930
all the way to the couplet.

17
00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.010
Your mission: explain why
Shakespeare ends on 'If'.
